---
layout: changelog
title: "Update custom domains on Sites and Functions"
date: 2026-11-25
cover: /images/blog/announcing-domain-updates/cover.avif
tags: sites, functions, domains, console, api
---

You can now change what a custom domain on Appwrite Sites or Functions serves, without deleting it and adding it again. Open the **Domains** tab, click **Update** in the domain's menu, and pick what it should serve.

A domain can switch between the active deployment and a branch, or move to a different branch. A redirect domain can point to a new URL or use a different status code. The domain keeps working while you change it, and its DNS records and certificate stay as they are.

You can make the same changes from your server with the Appwrite SDKs.

